 (names values)←resolveMsgBoxBtns(names values);lc;style
⍝ Derive a MsgBox's buttons from its Style when the application did not name
⍝ them, which is the usual case.
⍝
⍝ ⎕WC does this itself -- verified against Dyalog 20.0:
⍝
⍝     Style     ⎕WG'Btns'
⍝     Msg       OK
⍝     Info      OK
⍝     Query     YES  NO
⍝     Warn      OK   CANCEL
⍝     Error     OK   CANCEL
⍝
⍝ Without it every message box inherits the class default of a single 'OK', so
⍝ a Query box -- "do you really want to redeal?" -- offers no way to say no.
⍝ The client renders one button per element of Btns, and with Btns absent
⍝ altogether it renders a single button with no caption at all.
⍝
⍝ Sent as a nested vector of strings rather than the character matrix ⎕WG
⍝ returns, because that is what serialises usefully and what the client's
⍝ Array.isArray path expects.
 lc←⎕C names
 :If (⊂'btns')∊lc ⋄ →0 ⋄ :EndIf          ⍝ application named them; leave alone
 :If ~(⊂'style')∊lc ⋄ →0 ⋄ :EndIf        ⍝ no Style: class default 'OK' stands
 style←⎕C(lc⍳⊂'style')⊃values
 :Select style
 :Case 'query'
     names,←⊂'Btns' ⋄ values,←⊂'Yes' 'No'
 :CaseList 'warn' 'error'
     names,←⊂'Btns' ⋄ values,←⊂'OK' 'Cancel'
 :EndSelect
